how do we do a boolean when working with dataframes?

we use 

.isna()


.isna() checks every value:

True  → missing
False → not missing



   order_id  status  total
0     False   False  False
1     False   False   True
2     False   False  False
3     False   False  False
4     False   False   True





Using orders, print a Boolean Series showing which rows are duplicates.


print(orders.duplicated())


False → row is not a duplicate
True  → row repeats an earlier row


duplicated()
→ checks each original row
→ returns one True/False value per row
→ therefore the result is a Boolean Series





print(orders.drop_duplicates())


.drop_duplicates() removes repeated rows and returns a cleaned DataFrame.







Using orders, count how many times each value appears in the status column.


print(orders["status"].value_counts())


value_counts() counts how many times each unique value appears in the selected Series.






To count missing values in each column, use:

print(orders.isna().sum())